      "FR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-005 The stop gate enforces and never closes turns.",
      "- FR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-005-AC001 Blocks with `turn_in_progress` when a delivered request in the stop ledger (FR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-003-AC004) is still in progress; a withdrawn request still in progress blocks under AC009, and a minted request still `queued` only warns. A request in state `queued` (minted, not yet delivered) never produces `turn_in_progress`; the gate warns, naming its requestId and enqueue time. A Stop in one host session never blocks or warns on another host session's turns (`StopGate_OtherHostSession_NeverBlocksOrWarns`). A request enters the stop ledger when it is delivered, so a request minted before a passing Stop and delivered after it is evaluated at the next Stop (`StopGate_EnqueueR2_PassForR1_DequeueR2_NextStopBlocksUntilClosed`, including a restart between the two Stops). Unsupported-session failsafe: in a host session with `unsupportedSince` (whatever its reason, host binding table unsupported-session rule), every session-log write the model makes for a turn of that host session still in progress when `unsupportedSince` was recorded (a delivered open request, or a `withdrawn` queue entry still `in_progress`, addressed by its original pair; a minted request still `queued` is not covered and stays a warning) (evidence actions, design decisions, `requestClass`, and the close call; a review is never captured, keeping the no-failsafe rule of TR-MCP-SESSIONREVIEW-005 AC-002 and S9, and is refused with `turn_logging_unsupported`) is captured as a plugin failsafe record that carries the turn's C4 binding and root-id envelope, is marked `unsupported_session`, and is never sent to the server during that host session; every mint and every write for any other turn stays refused with `turn_logging_unsupported` and captures nothing (`UnsupportedSession_MintOrWriteForOtherTurn_Refused_NothingCaptured`). The Stop gate evaluates such a turn with its captured records counted: it blocks until the model's close is captured, with a remedy that names only the missing model evidence, the missing `requestClass` (from S8/S9, when the plugin's requestClass verb ships; a class write is captured like any other write), and the close call (all accepted, AC002; the plugin pre-check lets that close through, FR-MCP-SESSIONCLASS-004-AC002), because only the completion gate's terminal reviews cannot be written in that session; it then only warns with the cause and the retained failsafe records. The completion gate is judged at the drain: the server's gate judges the drained close, and a gate rejection keeps the turn in progress and listed with its original pair at that SessionStart, where its reviews are recorded through the C5 pair (FR-MCP-SESSIONREVIEW-002-AC002) before it is closed (`UnsupportedSession_ReviewRefused_NotCaptured`, `UnsupportedSession_CodeTurn_DrainedCloseRejectedByGate_StaysListed_ReviewViaPair_ThenCloses`). The next SessionStart for the agent drains the captured records in original order through the trusted recovery flow with the turn's original (MCP `sessionId`, `requestId`) pair (C5); a record whose turn is no longer in progress on the server is retained and warned, never forced. Each reason is covered from an earlier open turn (`StopGate_UnknownBridgeRecord_EarlierOpenTurn_CloseCaptured_ThenWarnsOnly`, `StopGate_TruncatedTranscript_EarlierOpenTurn_CloseCaptured_ThenWarnsOnly`, `StopGate_SyntheticUnsupportedSince_AnyReason_EarlierOpenTurn_CloseCaptured_ThenWarnsOnly` in A7; the real duplicate-hook transition `DuplicateHookAfterDelivery_UnsupportedSince_OpenTurnCloseCaptured` for copilot in A9 and `nodeDuplicateHookAfterDelivery_unsupportedSince_openTurnCloseCaptured` for classic cline in A8). A withdrawn-before-delivery turn is covered too: its decision, its `requestClass` (from S8/S9), and `failTurn` by original pair are captured, the next Stop warns instead of blocking, and the drain closes it (after S10 the server gate accepts that fail, which needs only the class) (`StopGate_WithdrawnBeforeDelivery_ThenUns