urn`); a hook-originated `mintTurn` without `MCP_PLUGIN_HOOK_INVOCATION=1` is refused by the plugin wrapper with `mint_requires_host_ingress` (`MintVerb_WithoutHookInvocation_RefusedMintRequiresHostIngress`); a payload missing its host row's nonce field reports `turn-open-failed` with `nonce_source_missing`, invents no nonce, and writes the failsafe diagnostic (`NonceSourceMissing_TurnOpenFailed_FailsafeDiagnostic`); slash command opens; contended lock reports `turn-open-contended` and calls no mint (`ContendedTurnOpenLock_ReportsTurnOpenContended_NoMint`); failed open retried; arrival bridge on a fixture transcript: an `enqueue` line mints once, a restart resumes from the stored offset without re-minting,  bridge cases on synthetic fixtures (run in both P0.2 branches), the real captured Claude Code prompt-form fixture case `Bridge_PromptFormsFixture_OneMintPerMessage` only when P0.2's claude-code prompt-form and head probes pass (otherwise `ClaudeCode_P0_2NotPassed_TurnLoggingUnsupported_ZeroMintsZeroWrites`), and, only when P0.2's Cowork hook and bridge probes pass, the same fixtures captured from Cowork (`Bridge_Cowork_PromptFormsFixture_OneMintPerMessage`, `Bridge_Cowork_DequeueTakesHead`); when they fail or are unavailable, A3 instead runs the unsupported-host case `Cowork_P0_2NotPassed_TurnLoggingUnsupported_ZeroMintsZeroWrites`, and the portable bridge cases stay unconditional; the P0.2 outcome that selected the branch is the feature-matrix receipt, `Bridge_UnequalRepresentations_DequeueDeliversHead`, `Bridge_TwoEqualTextMessages_TwoMints`, `Bridge_CrashBeforeAndAfterReplace_OneMint`, `Bridge_RestartReplay_NoReMint`, `Bridge_StalePid_Restarts`, `IdleEnded_ThenMidTurnMessage_MintedAtEnqueue`, `Bridge_ForkedTranscriptWithHistory_NoReMint`, `Bridge_TruncatedTranscript_WarnsNoChange`, `Bridge_DequeueNotHead_Or_PromptNotEnqueued_TurnLoggingUnsupported`, `RootIds_SystemEntryAndUnsupportedSince_SessionEnvelope_AfterWriteAndReplay`, mint-adapter cases `Mint404_BoundMintEndpoint_NoDetailCode_OutageClass_RetainedThenDrainedAfterServerUpgrade`, `MintVerb_StructuredUnknownMethodOrMethodNotFound_OutageClass_Deferred`, `Mint404_SessionNotOpen_Final_TurnOpenFailed`, `OutageSpanningSessionStart_DrainOpensSessionThenMints_NotFinal` (the drain replays the idempotent session open for the record's envelope `mcpSessionId` before the mint, and `session_not_open` is final only after that open is confirmed), `Rollback_OlderServer_MintsRetained_DrainAfterRestore`, and negative cases `Mint404_UnrelatedRoute_Final`, `Mint404_MalformedDetailMetadata_Final`, `MintVerb_ProseOnlyUnknownMethod_Final` (each asserts the server receives exactly one mint per message), `remove` with `absorbed_mid_turn` delivers and moves the write target, `remove` without that reason and `popAll` withdraw and leave the write target unchanged, a `dequeue` delivers a `kind: request` head and makes it the write target while a `kind: system` head delivers nothing (`Bridge_SystemEnqueueAheadOfUser_SystemDequeue_UserStaysQueued`, `Bridge_SystemEnqueue_Removed_NoTurn`, `Bridge_SystemAndUserInterleaved_CrashReplay_ZeroWrongTurnWrites`, whose zero-wrong-turn-writes half runs in A4), `Sync-PluginArrivalLog` given a recorded transcript length applies exactly the complete records ending at or before it, and no later record (`SyncArrivalLog_AppliesOnlyRecordsUpToRecordedLength`; the verb-side binding that uses it is an A4 case), the prompt hook mints and claims nothing on claude-code (`PromptHook_ClaudeCode_NoMintNoClaim`), `<task-notification>` and `<agent-message>` enqueues mint nothing, an unknown operation or a record missing a required field stops the bridge before it, without advancing `appliedThroughOffset`, and turn logging reports `turn_logging_unsupported` and, after a delivered request, records `unsupportedSince` with `arrival_bridge_format_unrecognized` (`Bridge_UnknownShape_StopsBeforeIt_NoSkip_Unsupported`, `Bridge_UnknownShapeOrTruncation_AfterDelivery_RecordsUnsupported