      "A4 MCP-SESSIONTURN-004 Independent per-turn edits and no-cancel. Reqs SESSIONTURN-003, -007, -001 (mid-turn AC). Contract: per-turn store and locks (above); `Get-PluginHostSessionKey` (host binding table), including the `CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID` verb-key read that replaces `CLAUDE_SESSION_ID` (`agent-runtime-header.ps1:165-169`) and the grok and grok-bot `sessionId` hook key; the verb-key env reads P0.2 selected (`CODEX_THREAD_ID` for codex, `GROK_SESSION_ID` for grok and grok-bot), each only when its P0.2 row selected it, else that host's verbs use the live-session rule; the SessionEnd hook's `sessions/<key>/ended.yaml` writer (`reason: session_end`); the SessionStart write of the host session's own `mcpSessionId` into `sessions/<key>/turn-state.yaml`, which the bridge, the mint, and every verb read as their only MCP session id source (the workspace-level `session-state.yaml` becomes a legacy file not used for targeting, and the rotated-sessionId rebind at `repl-invoke.ps1:1954-1965` is not applied to per-turn files), and SessionStart's application of pending transcript records through `Sync-PluginArrivalLog` up to the transcript length at its start (TR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-003 AC-007); `New-ReplInvocationBinding`; `Resolve-ReplTargetTurn`; `Register-ReplOpenTurn`; `Add-ReplStopLedgerEntry`; delete `Invoke-ReplSupersedeCurrentTurnIfInProgress`; every verb (appendActions, appendDialog, updateTurn, completeTurn, failTurn, setTurnTitle, recordReview later) resolves exactly one target and mutates only it; failsafe and fingerprint namespaced by requestId; `failTurn` keeps the file (cleanup by stop gate). RED (SessionTurnIntegrity, Describe isolation): using A3's `Sync-PluginArrivalLog`, a verb started after a `dequeue` line was written binds to that request even before the bridge applies it (`Binding_VerbDrainsTranscriptBeforeBinding`), and a `dequeue` appended after the verb started but before it took the lock leaves it bound to the earlier request (`Binding_DequeueAppendedAfterStartBeforeLock_BindsToEarlier`); a new mint leaves prior turn in_progress locally and on the server and persists no `canceled` (`Isolation_NewMint_NeverPersistsCanceledForOtherTurn`, `Isolation_HooksNeverPersistCanceled`); explicit requestId targets an earlier turn, and `setTurnTitle` with an explicit requestId retitles only that turn (`SetTurnTitle_ExplicitRequestId_TargetsThatTurn`); per-turn identity holds across open turns (`Binding_PerTurnIdentity_AcrossOpenTurns`); unknown id refused; a verb with no write target is refused with `request_unknown` naming the host session key (`Binding_NoWriteTarget_RequestUnknown_NamesHostSessionKey`); after a failed open, unqualified verbs are refused with `request_unknown` (`Binding_AfterFailedOpen_UnqualifiedVerb_RequestUnknown`); with the write target closed while an earlier delivered request is open, an unqualified verb is refused with `turn_immutable` naming it (`Binding_WriteTargetClosed_EarlierStillOpen_TurnImmutable`); a legacy failsafe record without a captured binding is retained and never auto-replayed (`Failsafe_LegacyUnbound_NeverAutoReplayed_Retained`), and a turn in progress in the legacy `current-turn.yaml` is listed at the first SessionStart and stays addressable by explicit requestId (`LegacyCurrentTurnInProgress_ListedAtFirstSessionStart_AddressableByRequestId`); a same-nonce `merged` mint for a terminal turn is neither write target, open, nor ledgered (`PromptHook_SameNonceTerminalTurn_Merged_NotTargetNotOpenNotLedger`); the host-session key reads (`HostSessionKey_ClaudeCodeSessionIdEnv_AndGrokCamelCaseSessionId_Read`; for codex, grok, and grok-bot, each under the P0.2 gating rule, the verb-key env its P0.2 row selected, else the live-session rule: `HostSessionKey_P0_2SelectedVerbEnv_CodexGrokGrokBot_ElseLiveSessionRule`); for codex, P0.2's recorded payloads of a running turn A and of each mid-turn message B (every TUI way and `codex queue`), replayed through the prompt hook, mint one turn per message, each B its own turn with its own `turn_id` nonce while A stays open and unchanged (`Codex_MidTurnMessages_RecordedPayloads_DistinctTurnIds_OwnTurns`) and the SessionEnd marker (`SessionEnd_WritesEndedMarker_ReasonSessionEnd`); idle revival (`IdleEnded_KeyedVerb_RevivesAtomically_NoTargetRequestUnknown`, `IdleEnded_Revival_CrashRestart_Consistent`, `SessionEndMarker_NeverRevives`); the verb-side halves of A3's bridge and fail-closed cases, same names and fixtures (every session-log verb refused with `turn_logging_unsupported`, zero server writes, zero wrong-turn writes: `Bridge_EqualContentRemoval_FailsClosed_SessionUnsupported_ZeroWrites`, `Bridge_EqualContentPopAll_FewerLines_FailsClosed`, `Bridge_UnknownShape_StopsBeforeIt_NoSkip_Unsupported`, `Bridge_UnknownShapeOrTruncation_AfterDelivery_RecordsUnsupportedSince`, `Bridge_DequeueNotHead_Or_PromptNotEnqueued_TurnLoggingUnsupported`, `Bridge_FailClosed_CursorNotAdvanced_RestartStaysUnsupported`, `Bridge_SystemAndUserInterleaved_CrashReplay_ZeroWrongTurnWrites`, `Copilot_EqualFieldsSecondInvocation_FailsClosed_NoSecondMint`, and whichever `*_P0_2NotPassed_TurnLoggingUnsupported_ZeroMintsZeroWrites` cases A3 ran); concurrent `Start-Job` edits to two turns (actions, title, decisions) produce exact per-turn results with no cross-contamination and no lost updates; completing one turn leaves the other untouched; failsafe for turn A never replays onto turn B; a prompt-hook or arrival-bridge mint mid-turn registers without cancel; the model-facing verb and tool lists contain no mint verb (`mintTurn` is called only by hooks and adapters, D6); `PerTurnTitle_NeverOverwritesAnotherTurnsTitle` (TR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-003-AC005: a refined title on turn A survives title, re-submit, and close operations on turn B); binding tests (`Binding_VerbAfterSecondEnqueue_BeforeDelivery_WritesToFirstTurn`, `Binding_TwoDeliveredOpen_NoRequestId_RefusedAmbiguous`, `Binding_R1R2R1_WithRequestIds_EachOnOwnTurn`, `Binding_AfterR1Closed_UnqualifiedVerbWritesToR2`, `Binding_SecondDequeued_FirstClosed_WritesToSecondTurn`, `Binding_WithdrawnRequest_NeverBecomesWriteTarget`, `Binding_ExplicitRequestIdOverride_WritesToEarlierTurn`, `Binding_FailsafeReplay_UsesCapturedBinding_NotCurrentActive`, `Binding_NoKey_SingleLiveSession_BindsWithInferredWarning`, `Binding_NoKey_NoLiveSession_RefusedUnknown`, `Binding_NoKey_TwoLiveSessions_RefusedAmbiguous_ZeroWrongTurnWrites`, `Binding_NoKey_TrustedPair_RecoveryFlow_Accepted`, `Binding_NoKey_RequestIdOnly_Refused`, `Binding_NoKey_PairFromOtherConversation_Refused`, `Binding_ExplicitRequestId_OtherMcpSession_RefusedRequestUnknown`, `Binding_ClaudeClear_ShellVerbUsesNewSession`, `Binding_ClaudeClear_LongLivedProcessResolvesPerCall`, `Binding_ClaudeResume_UsesResumedSessionKey`, `Binding_TwoHostSessions_NeverShareActiveRequest`, `Binding_CurrentTurnYaml_NeverUsedForTargeting`, `RootIds_EveryRecordFamily_PresentAfterWriteAndReplay`, `TwoHostSessions_OwnMcpSessionIds_SecondSessionStartNeverRetargetsFirst`). Requirement-refinement updates to existing supersede expectations in `SessionLogReviewRegression.Tests.ps1`, `PluginPowerShellRuntime.Tests.ps1`, `SessionLogP2Contracts.Tests.ps1`, `TriagePluginIdentity.Tests.ps1` (recorded as RequirementRefined). Gates G4, G2, G5 (the `PluginSessionLogIntegration` cases for this slice's behavior, `NewPrompt_DoesNotCancelPriorTurn_ServerStatusInProgress` and `ConcurrentTurnEdits_AreIsolated`, are A9's, because that fixture runs the sibling plugin repos, `PluginSessionLogWorkflowAdapter.ResolvePluginRoot`, which receive the new core only at A9's sync). The verb-side halves of the A3 `<Host>_P0_2NotPassed_TurnLoggingUnsupported_ZeroMintsZeroWrites` cases (ClaudeCode, Grok, GrokBot, Copilot, Cowork) run here under the same names: every session-log verb reports `turn_logging_unsupported` and writes nothing.",
      "A5 MCP-SESSIONTURN-005 Truthful plugin receipts. Reqs SESSIONTURN-004 (plugin ACs). Contract: `Get-ReplTurnWriteOutcome`; receipt `-Code -StoredStatus`; `Invoke-ReplPersistTurn` fails loudly on `skipped_terminal`; cached terminal status refuses verbs locally (`turn_immutable`); the close verbs remove a request from the open delivered list and the stop ledger only when the mapped outcome confirms the server close (TR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-003 AC-007); the A3 alias rebind is extended to real queued writes through `Invoke-ReplPersistTurn`. RED: SessionTurnIntegrity Describe R4 (mocked `Invoke-ReplRaw` outcomes: `Outcomes_SkippedTerminal_PersistedFalse_ExitNonZero`, `Outcomes_PerTurnMapping_FromServerTurns`; a queued, refused, or failed close leaves the request open and ledgered while a confirmed close removes it (`CloseVerb_OnlyServerConfirmedClose_LeavesOpenListAndLedger`); the drain rebinds real queued writes in original order through the persist path, and each A3 crash boundary loses no write (`AliasRebind_QueuedWrites_OriginalOrder_ThroughPersistPath`, `AliasJournal_CrashBoundaries_OneMintNoLostWrite` with real queued writes)). The `PluginSessionLogIntegration` case for this slice's outcome, `AppendActionsToCanceledTurn_ReportsSkippedTerminal_ServerHasZeroActions`, is A9's for the same reason as A4's. Gates G4, G2, G5.",
      "A6 MCP-SESSIONTURN-006 Decision lists through verbs. Contract: `New-McpPluginTurnUpsertRequest` (`McpPluginShim.psm1:386-482`) adds `-DesignDecisions -RequirementsDiscovered -Blockers`; pass-through and fingerprint (`repl-invoke.ps1:1645-1663`); verb params; model-evidence counters exclude hook invocations; `appendDecisions` writes the C7 triple with idempotent replay (today it writes only the `designDecisions` entry). RED: the serialize test at `PluginPowerShellRuntime.Tests.ps1:1315` (Pester test name 'TEST-MCP-PLUGIN-PSONLY-001 imports shim module and serializes DTO contracts with PowerShell-native JSON'; a test name, not a requirement id) and documented-members list (the `New-McpPluginTurnUpsertRequest` entry of the documented-members table); SessionTurnIntegrity decision tests (`AppendDecisions_WritesTriple_ReplayIdempotent`, `IncidentalResubmit_DecisionListVerbs_OmitTitle`). Gates G4, G2, G3, G5.",
      "A7 MCP-SESSIONTURN-007 Stop gate enforcement. Reqs SESSIONTURN-005. Contract: `Get-PluginStopGateTurns` (IO; it first applies pending transcript records through `Sync-PluginArrivalLog` up to the transcript length at the Stop's start, from the payload `transcript_path`), `Get-PluginStopGateFindings` (pure), `Close-PluginTurnIfNeeded` rewritten (lines 993-1031 auto-close removed); the close verbs `completeTurn` and `failTurn` refuse a turn with no model-authored action, design decision, or commit with `turn_missing_model_evidence`, leaving it in progress (FR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-005-AC002; A6's counters, hook invocations excluded, commits counted per TR-MCP-PLUGIN-011-AC003); the Stop hook reads the payload `stop_hook_active` (Claude Code) or `stopHookActive` (Grok, grok-bot) instead of the env `CLAUDE_STOP_HOOK_ACTIVE` (`plugin-hook.ps1:944`). RED: SessionTurnIntegrity Describe R5 (the unsupported-session failsafe cases `StopGate_EqualFieldFailClosed_EarlierOpenTurn_CloseCapturedToFailsafe_ThenWarnsOnly_DrainsWithOriginalPair` and `StopGate_BridgeAmbiguity_EarlierOpenTurn_CloseCapturedToFailsafe_ThenWarnsOnly_DrainsWithOriginalPair`: an earlier delivered turn is open when the session fails closed, Stop blocks with the reduced remedy (only the missing model evidence and the close call; from S8/S9 also the missing `requestClass`, and S8 updates these cases' expected remedy accordingly as a RequirementRefined decision), the model's evidence and close calls are captured as `unsupported_session` failsafe records and nothing reaches the server, the next Stop warns and does not block, a restart keeps the records and the original (`sessionId`, `requestId`), and the next SessionStart drains them through the trusted recovery flow so the server shows the turn closed with that evidence; `UnsupportedSession_MintOrWriteForOtherTurn_Refused_NothingCaptured`; the same from an earlier open turn for an unknown bridge record and a truncated transcript (`StopGate_UnknownBridgeRecord_EarlierOpenTurn_CloseCaptured_ThenWarnsOnly`, `StopGate_TruncatedTranscript_EarlierOpenTurn_CloseCaptured_ThenWarnsOnly`), and for a synthetic `unsupportedSince` with any other reason (`StopGate_SyntheticUnsupportedSince_AnyReason_EarlierOpenTurn_CloseCaptured_ThenWarnsOnly`; the real duplicate-hook transition is an A8 and A9 case); before S10 the server has no completion gate, so A7 asserts only capture, the Stop warning, and a drain the server accepts (the review refusal is tested in S8 and S9, the gate-rejected drain in S10); each block/warn row incl. two consecutive Stop invocations with a still-open turn, the second carrying `stop_hook_active=true`, both blocking and a pass after the model closes the turn, a host-forced stop recording `stop_gate_overridden_by_host`, a request minted before a passing Stop and delivered after it blocking the next Stop until closed, across a restart (`StopGate_EnqueueR2_PassForR1_DequeueR2_NextStopBlocksUntilClosed`), and a crash injected before and after the atomic replace that delivers a request never leaves the ledger and the cursor disagreeing (`StopGate_DeliveryCrashBoundaries_LedgerAndCursorAgree`), and a passing Stop clears only confirmed-closed ledger entries while preserving the queue, cursor, `unsupportedSince`, and a concurrent delivery, across a crash (`StopGate_PassClearsOnlyEligibleLedgerEntries_PreservesStateAcrossCrash`), `turn_withdrawn_unclosed` for a withdrawn in-progress request and none once the model has failed it, `duplicate_delivery_suspected` for two mints within 2 s with equal prompt hash and none for 2.1 s or differing hash, the gate blocks while a request turn opened since the last Stop is in progress and never calls completeTurn or failTurn (`StopGate_BlocksDeliveredInProgress_WithdrawnSeparately_QueuedWarnsOnly`, `StopGate_NeverCompletesOrFailsTurn`), the findings function does no IO (`StopGateFindings_IsPure_NoIo`), hook-authored actions not evidence, the failed-build regression (the existing Pester test at `PluginPowerShellRuntime.Tests.ps1:2512`); a model close held in the ordinary failsafe by a transport outage turns the block into the degraded persistence warning while its ledger entry stays until the server confirms the close (`StopGate_OutageCloseQueued_WarnsDegraded_LedgerKeptUntilConfirmed`); with the arrival bridge dead, the Stop hook applies pending transcript records up to the transcript length at its start (payload `transcript_path`) and blocks on a request delivered but unclosed (`StopGate_BridgeDead_AppliesPendingRecords_BlocksDeliveredUnclosed`); the close-verb evidence rule and remedies (`CloseVerb_NoEvidence_Refused_TurnStaysInProgress`, `CloseVerb_CommitOnlyEvidence_Accepted`, `StopGate_ClosedWithoutEvidenceElsewhere_WarnsOnly`, `StopGate_EveryBlockRemedy_AcceptedOnBlockedTurnStatus`, `StopGate_WithdrawnFailedPerInstruction_NextStopPasses`, `StopGate_EachRemedyFollowedLiterally_NextStopPasses`); the ledger is exactly the requests delivered since the last passing Stop plus every entry whose close the server has not confirmed, and the gate evaluates it together with the separate scan of `withdrawn` entries still `in_progress` (a request minted from `enqueue` and withdrawn by `popAll` before any delivery leaves the ledger empty, is blocked as `turn_withdrawn_unclosed`, and after it is failed by its original pair the next Stop passes; the block survives a restart and never appears in another host session: `StopGate_WithdrawnBeforeDelivery_EmptyLedger_BlocksWithdrawnUnclosed_FailByPair_NextStopPasses`), and a turn the server reports terminal from another surface leaves the open list (`StopGate_LedgerListsDeliveredSinceLastPass_PlusUnconfirmedCloses`, `StopGate_TurnClosedElsewhere_DroppedFromOpenList`, `StopGate_QueuedInProgressServerTurn_NoBlockBeforeDelivery_Warns`; a withdrawn-before-delivery turn later caught by `unsupportedSince` is captured by its original pair, warned, and closed at the drain, with restart and other-host-session negatives: `St